{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `r_safestan_flat`, a deterministic flattened expansion of the compressed LSAT response patterns.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the original likelihood scores `r[k]`, where `r` is transformed data constructed from `response` and `culm`. SafeStan requires observed variables on the left side of `~` to be top-level protected data and not indexed. I added `r_safestan_flat` as top-level data and replaced the loop of indexed Bernoulli-logit sampling statements with one vectorized sampling statement. The deterministic relation is `r_safestan_flat[(k - 1) * N + j] = r[k, j]`, where `r` is the expanded response array defined by the original transformed-data construction. The existing built-in priors for `alpha`, `theta`, and `beta` were retained.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N; // 1000, number of students
  int<lower=0> R; // 32, number of patterns of results: 2^T
  int<lower=0> T; // 5, number of questions
  array[R] int<lower=0> culm;
  array[R, T] int<lower=0> response;
  array[T * N] int<lower=0> r_safestan_flat;
}
parameters {
  array[T] real alpha;
  vector[N] theta;
  real<lower=0> beta;
}
model {
  vector[T * N] eta;

  alpha ~ normal(0, 100.);
  theta ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta ~ normal(0.0, 100.);

  for (k in 1 : T) {
    for (j in 1 : N) {
      eta[(k - 1) * N + j] = beta * theta[j] - alpha[k];
    }
  }
  r_safestan_flat ~ bernoulli_logit(eta);
}
generated quantities {
  real mean_alpha;
  array[T] real a;
  mean_alpha = mean(alpha);
  for (t in 1 : T) {
    a[t] = alpha[t] - mean_alpha;
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":4,"R":3,"T":1,"culm":[2,2,1],"response":[[3],[3],[1]],"r_safestan_flat":[3,3,1,1]}","protected_variables":["r_safestan_flat"]}
